SANS @RISK: Critical Threat Briefing
Volume 24, Issue 38

NOTABLE VULNERABILITY SUMMARY:
Vulnerability: CVE-2024-21626
Vendor: Open Containers Initiative / runc
Product: runc Container Runtime
Affected Versions: runc versions prior to 1.1.12
Vulnerability Type: Container Escape / Privilege Escalation
Attack Vector: NETWORK / LOCAL EXECUTION
MITRE ATT&CK Technique: T1068 (Exploitation for Privilege Escalation)
Threat Actor: Undisclosed Threat Group (UNC-4841 Activity)
Exploitation Status: ACTIVE_IN_THE_WILD
Attack Outcome: SUCCESSFUL EXPLOITATION OBSERVED
Affected Sector: Cloud Infrastructure, Healthcare, Enterprise Financials
Publication Date: 2026-09-16

EXECUTIVE ANALYSIS:
Security researchers and telemetry sources confirm active in-the-wild exploitation of CVE-2024-21626. Threat actors are leveraging an internal file descriptor leak in runc to escape container boundaries and compromise host operating systems (Linux kernels on AWS and hybrid clusters). Successful exploitation grants root privileges on the hosting node, enabling lateral movement and sensitive credential theft.

RECOMMENDED CONTROLS & REMEDIATION:
- Upgrade runc to version 1.1.12 or later across all containerized workloads.
- NIST-PR.AC-1: Enforce strict access control hardening and host-level container sandboxing.
- CIS Control 4.1: Isolate management planes and public-facing container hosts.

POTENTIAL BUSINESS IMPACT:
High risk of full cluster takeover and intellectual property exfiltration. Financial impact estimated at ₹2,500,000 to ₹5,000,000 per affected production server.

